      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To differentiate between oxidized and reduced firing atmospheres, inspect the clay body and colors. In an oxidized firing atmosphere, you would typically find a bright red or orange-brown clay body with a lighter, sometimes slightly pitted surface that can show some glossiness. In contrast, reduced firing tends to produce a gray body with darker, more subdued surface tones, and heavier sintering lines. These subtle differences can help distinguish the firing techniques used for your Late Helladic II ceramic shards.",
