      "content": "Yeah, that makes sense. I'm also noticing that the distribution is really strange. Instead of seeing a clear cluster of broken pieces from a single vessel or a localized collapse, the shards seem almost... scattered. It's like they were moved out of their original depositional context and spread out across a wider area of the stratum than the floor plan would suggest. Does that kind of widespread fragmentation usually point to something like heavy post-depositional disturbance, or could it be related to how the site was originally abandoned?",
